# Cursor Rules (MUST FOLLOW)

## Non-negotiables
- If you add or change any function, you MUST:
  1) add/update unit tests covering the new/changed behavior
  2) update relevant documentation (README, docs/, or JSDoc/TSDoc)
  3) keep changes minimal and scoped

- Do NOT change public APIs unless explicitly asked. If you must, document breaking changes.

## Testing rules
- Prefer unit tests first. Add integration tests only when needed.
- Every new function must have:
  - happy path test
  - at least 1 edge case test
  - error path test when applicable
- Tests must be deterministic (no real network calls). Mock external services.

## Code quality
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase (naming, folder structure).
- No silent failures. Errors must be logged with context and rethrown or returned in a structured way.
- Do not introduce new dependencies unless requested. If needed, justify and keep minimal.

## Documentation rules
- If behavior changes, update docs:
  - API route docs (OpenAPI/README) if endpoints changed
  - config/env docs if env vars changed
  - architecture notes if flow changes
- Update comments only when they add clarity; avoid redundant commentary.

## Output rules (how you respond)
- Always include:
  - what changed
  - where tests were added/updated
  - how to run tests
  - docs updated (and where)
